  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5285559cfa33d7041aa12c3287c4d2a7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 05_READING_THE_DIAGNOSTIC_CONSOLE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NotebookSection
  number: 05
  title: READING THE DIAGNOSTIC CONSOLE
  unlocked: 1
  entries:
  - title: Syndrome table
    tag: 1
    body: "Use the syndrome bits in the order shown in entry 17 (first bit = lamp
      A, second bit = lamp B).\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>SYND  PAIR q0,q1  PAIR q1,q2 
      ACTION</b></color>\n 00   agree       agree       No correction\n 10   differ     
      agree       X on q0\n 11   differ      differ      X on q1\n 01   agree      
      differ      X on q2\n\n<color=#3fe0b5><b>\u258C IN THIS INVESTIGATION</b>\n<indent=0.9em>The
      console's syndrome comes from the circuit's <b>measured</b> parity checks.
      It is produced by the simulation, not assigned by the story.</indent></color>"
    bench: 3
    qiskit: 'FIX = {"00": None, "10": 0, "11": 1, "01": 2}

      fix = FIX[syndrome]  
      # which data qubit to flip'
  - title: Why the syndrome finds the error
    tag: 1
    body: "Start from the encoded state |000\u27E9 and flip one qubit:\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>FLIPPED 
      DATA  q0vsq1  q1vsq2  SYNDROME  FIX</b></color>\n  none     000   agree   agree    
      00      none\n  q0       100   differ  agree     10      X on q0\n  q1      
      010   differ  differ    11      X on q1\n  q2       001   agree   differ   
      01      X on q2\n\n<color=#ffe2a8><b>\u258C INTUITION: THE LAMP RULE</b>\n<indent=0.9em>Find
      the qubit that sits in <b>every</b> pair that differs and in <b>no</b> pair
      that agrees. For syndrome 10, only the first pair differs, and q0 is the only
      qubit that belongs to the first pair alone. For 11, both pairs differ, and
      q1 is the only qubit in both pairs. For 01, only the second pair differs, which
      singles out q2.</indent></color>"
    bench: 3
    qiskit: 
  guides:
  - label: Bit-ordering in the Qiskit SDK
    url: https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/bit-ordering
  - label: Visualize results
    url: https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/visualize-results
